## Reviewer got wrong (not applied)

- bn-a row 1. The English “generally about 3 / 4 / 6 months” was already softened on purpose by R3. “কিছু রায়ে … কোনো নিশ্চিত বা সাধারণ ফল নয়” is that rule, not a mistranslation of a usual sentence into an uncommon one. Restoring সাধারণত would read as a typical sentence.
- bn-a row 19. Same advertising rule. “তথ্য ও প্রমাণ যে ক্ষতিপূরণ সমর্থন করে” is the required wording. The suggested “যত ক্ষতিপূরণ পাওয়া যায়” is the maximum-compensation claim R3 removed. It is advice about the work, but it is still a result-degree claim the rule forbids.
- bn-a row 16 and bn-b row 18 are culturally right about lakh grouping and about “TWD 1.57M” looking like an English abbreviation. They are not applicable here: the checker does not parse lakh/crore grouping, and the bio figure is pinned.
- bn-b row 9 is a real defect (U+200B, including lines whose only character is that space). It is not a wording mistake the fixer can remove: the block checker demands the same ZWSP count as the Korean source.
